5:   - The CLI JSON writer still serializes fold details without `gate_metadata`, `selection_source`, `used_fallback_candidates`, or `gate_passed_alphas` at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:326-343`. Static check: `gate_metadata in script: False`, `selection_source in script: False`.\n26: - Impact: Prior F1 required the fallback source label to survive `_compute_horizon_signal -> horizon_details -> FoldMetrics/JSON where applicable`. The in-memory multi-horizon path is partially fixed, but persisted JSON still cannot distinguish fallback-only candidates from actual Research Gate-passed alphas.\n27: - Required fix: Persist `m.gate_metadata` (or equivalent fold/horizon gate diagnostics) into `fold_details` JSON. If multi-horizon reporting remains first-horizon-only, the JSON must still carry the source label for the reported `gated_alphas`.\n28: \n29: ### F2 - BLOCKER - Required CLI parse/pass/persist test coverage still missing\n30: \n31: - Evidence:\n32:   - `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py` has no references to `run_phase35_backtest`, `argparse`, `phase35_backtest_results`, or `json.dump` (`0` matches each).\n33:   - The new `test_fold_metrics_includes_gate_metadata` is conditional: if `metrics.gate_metadata is not None`, it checks fields; if it is `None`, the test still passes at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:1183-1187`.\n34:   - Single-horizon `run_fold` explicitly sets `gate_metadata = None` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:2013-2014`, so the conditional test does not prove structural metadata is present.\n35: - Impact: Prior F2 explicitly required coverage for fallback labeling and CLI parse/pass/persist behavior. Fallback metadata unit coverage exists for direct `_compute_horizon_signal`, but script-level parse/pass/persist coverage is still absent, and the FoldMetrics test can pass without metadata.\n36: - Required fix: Add a real script-level or parser-helper test that verifies `--p10-gate-mode`, `--p10-gate-min-pass`, `--p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates` parse, are passed into `Phase35WalkForwardEngine`, and are persisted. Add an assertion that fold JSON includes fallback labeling when fallback candidates are used.\n37: \n38: ## Verified Passes\n39: \n40: - Default strict behavior unchanged: constructor defaults remain `p10_gate_mode=\"strict\"`, `p10_gate_min_pass=1`, `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates=False`; strict mode excludes zero-pass horizons at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1303-1307`; tests cover this at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:757-792`.\n41: - Relaxed mode opt-in only: CLI defaults to `strict` and requires explicit `--p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates` at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:117-132`; relaxed fallback candidates are only admitted inside `self.p10_gate_mode == \"relaxed\"` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1308-1331`.\n42: - FAIL strings are not counted as pass: robust verdict checks reject `FAIL*`, `REJECT*`, `NEEDS_FIX*`; tests cover this at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:491-575`.\n43: - Fallback-only candidates are not treated as gate-passed in `_compute_horizon_signal`: fallback metadata reports `selection_source='fallback_candidate'`, `used_fallback_candidates=True`, `gate_passed_count=0`, and empty `gate_passed_alphas`; tests cover the direct function path at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:1017-1078`.\n44: - Final-objective signed weighting still blocks negative/zero quality: single surviving non-positive quality returns `None`; all non-positive quality returns `None`; no `abs()` or equal-weight fallback is used in `_blend_horizon_signals` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1509-1539`; tests cover this at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:590-738` and `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:931-967`.\n45: - PIT safety/no lookahead regression: horizon gate and quality metrics are computed from embargoed train/validation slices at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1237-1292` and `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1394-1422`; no new test-period return usage was found in gate decisions or blend weights.\n46: \n47: ## Verification Run\n48: \n49: - `python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q`: 39 passed.\n50: - `python -m pytest tests/phase35/ -q`: 139 passed.\n51: - Static script JSON check: `gate_metadata in script: False`; `selection_source in script: False`; P10 config keys present.\n52: - Static test coverage check: `run_phase35_backtest: 0`, `argparse: 0`, `phase35_backtest_results: 0`, `json.dump: 0` in `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`.\n53: \n54: ## Final Verdict\n55: \n56: [NEEDS_FIX]\n57: \n58: The core PIT behavior and relaxed-mode opt-in controls remain acceptable, but F1/F2 are not fully closed because fallback labels are not persisted to JSON and required CLI parse/pass/persist tests are still absent.\n\n(End of file - total 58 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Role21 P10 Gate Tuning Fix Re-Audit - 2026-06-10\n\n## Gate Contract\n\n- l3_session_id: role21-p10-gate-tuning-fix-20260610T061200+0700\n- l3_session_key: codex:role21:p10-gate-tuning-fix:20260610T061200+0700\n- audit_report_path: .ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_fix_reaudit_20260610.md\n- final_verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n\n## Audit Header\n\n- Role: [L3-Audit:Role21-CodeReviewer]\n- Verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n- PIT Safety: PASS\n- Role Compliance: PASS\n- Scope: Re-audit of F1/F2 fixes from `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md` across `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, and `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_role21_fix_report_20260610.md`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1 - BLOCKER - Fallback labeling still does not survive persisted JSON artifacts","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_Q