{"type":"text","timestamp":1781048118267,"sessionID":"ses_15146aa59ffeFu5eiEqXVPGfdu","part":{"id":"prt_eaebd2ec2001wSy6RJOTZGhr74","messageID":"msg_eaebd2228001Gd4q4OWe8zfrLw","sessionID":"ses_15146aa59ffeFu5eiEqXVPGfdu","type":"text","text":"<thinking>\nHmm, that's a problem. The gate_metadata is NOT being persisted to the JSON file. Let me think about why this might be happening.\n\nLooking at the logs, I can see that the multi-horizon blend path was executed and fallback was triggered. The logs show:\n- `[P10] Horizon 1 complete: gated_alphas=5, own_val_ic=0.0000, final_obj_val_ic=0.0000, gate_passed=0/5, selection_source=fallback_candidate`\n- `[P10] Fold 1: Fallback complete. Reason: all_quality_non_positive, Requested horizons: [1, 3, 5], Successful horizons: [1, 3, 5]`\n\nBut then it fell back to the single-horizon baseline:\n- `WARNING:omega.quant.phase35_walk_forward:[P10] Fold 1: Blend returned None (all quality non-positive). Falling back to single-horizon baseline using return_col=fwd_ret_5`\n- `INFO:omega.quant.phase35_walk_forward:[P10] Fold 1: Executing fallback to single-horizon baseline (return_col=fwd_ret_5)`\n\nAnd according to the audit report at line 34:\n- \"Single-horizon `run_fold` explicitly sets `gate_metadata = None` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:2013-2014`, so the conditional test does not prove structural metadata is present.\"\n\nSo it seems like when the multi-horizon blend falls back to single-horizon baseline, it's calling `run_fold` which sets `gate_metadata = None`. That's why the JSON doesn't have gate_metadata.\n\nHowever, looking at the audit report at lines 23-25:\n- \"The multi-horizon caller stores that object in `horizon_details` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1659-1695` and copies only the first horizon's metadata into `FoldMetrics` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1755-1763`.\"\n\nSo the gate_metadata SHOULD be present when multi-horizon blend succeeds. But in our quick-mode test, it fell back to single-horizon baseline because all quality metrics were non-positive (smoke test mode with only 1 symbol).\n\nLet me check if the FoldMetrics actually has gate_metadata set in the multi-horizon path. I need to look at the phase35_walk_forward.py code to understand where gate_metadata is being set and why it might be None.\n\nActually, I should verify my implementation is correct. Let me check if the serialize_fold_details function is handling the case where gate_metadata is None correctly.\n\nLooking at my implementation:\n```python\ngate_meta = getattr(m, \"gate_metadata\", None)\nif gate_meta is not None:\n    # Store the full gate_metadata dict\n    fold_dict[\"gate_metadata\"] = gate_meta\n    ...\n```\n\nThis is correct - it only adds gate_metadata fields if gate_meta is not None. So the function is working as designed.\n\nThe issue is that in the quick-mode test, the multi-horizon blend fell back to single-horizon baseline, which explicitly sets gate_metadata = None (as mentioned in the audit report).\n\nTo properly test that gate_metadata is persisted, I would need to:\n1. Run a test where multi-horizon blend actually succeeds (not falls back)\n2. OR check the code to verify that gate_metadata is being set correctly in the multi-horizon path\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the audit report. The issue F1 states:\n- \"The CLI JSON writer still serializes fold details without `gate_metadata`, `selection_source`, `used_fallback_candidates`, or `gate_passed_alphas`\"\n\nBut the audit also says at line 24:\n- \"The multi-horizon caller stores that object in `horizon_details` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1659-1695` and copies only the first horizon's metadata into `FoldMetrics` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1755-1763`.\"\n\nSo the gate_metadata SHOULD be present on FoldMetrics when multi-horizon blend succeeds. The problem is just that it wasn't being serialized to JSON.\n\nMy fix is correct - I added serialize_fold_details() to handle gate_metadata when it's present. The fact that it's NOT present in this quick-mode run is expected because the blend fell back to single-horizon baseline.\n\nHowever, I should verify that my fix works when gate_metadata IS present. Let me check if there's a way to verify this, or if I need to write a more specific test that creates a FoldMetrics with gate_metadata and verifies the JSON output.\n\nActually, I already wrote that test! In my F2 tests, I have:\n- `test_serialize_fold_details_with_gate_metadata()` - This creates a mock FoldMetrics with gate_metadata and verifies it's serialized correctly.\n\nAnd the tests passed (42 tests passed). So my implementation should be correct.\n\nThe issue is that the quick-mode backtest fell back to single-horizon baseline, which doesn't set gate_metadata. But my implementation is correct and will persist gate_metadata when it's present.\n\nLet me verify by checking if my test actually ran and passed. Let me look at the test output more carefully.\n</thinking>\n\nThe gate_metadata is not in the JSON because the quick-mode backtest fell back to single-horizon baseline (which sets gate_metadata = None). However, my implementation is correct - it will persist gate_metadata when present. Let me verify my tests passed by checking the test count:","time":{"start":1781048094402,"end":1781048118265}}}
