{"type":"text","timestamp":1781048141329,"sessionID":"ses_15146aa59ffeFu5eiEqXVPGfdu","part":{"id":"prt_eaebdc8b5001rvCgDC9XWHEQbT","messageID":"msg_eaebda94a001d1L8J219c9qms1","sessionID":"ses_15146aa59ffeFu5eiEqXVPGfdu","type":"text","text":"<thinking>\nPerfect! All 3 of my F2 tests passed:\n1. `test_cli_parser_includes_p10_gate_config_keys` - Verified the script includes P10 gate config keys\n2. `test_serialize_fold_details_with_gate_metadata` - Verified serialize_fold_details() properly serializes gate_metadata when present\n3. `test_serialize_fold_details_without_gate_metadata` - Verified backward compatibility when gate_metadata is None\n\nSo my implementation is correct. The serialize_fold_details() function will persist gate_metadata to JSON when it's present on FoldMetrics.\n\nThe reason the quick-mode backtest didn't have gate_metadata in the JSON is because:\n1. Multi-horizon blend was executed with all 3 horizons\n2. All horizons used fallback candidates (gate_passed=0)\n3. All quality metrics were non-positive (smoke test with 1 symbol)\n4. The blend returned None and fell back to single-horizon baseline\n5. Single-horizon baseline explicitly sets gate_metadata = None\n\nThis is expected behavior for the quick-mode smoke test. The important thing is that my code will persist gate_metadata when it's present, which my tests verify.\n\nNow I need to write the L2 implementation report as specified in the prompt.\n</thinking>","time":{"start":1781048133813,"end":1781048141327}}}
